WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.910
A book with a title in unfamiliar letters
walks through a doorway marked translation.

2
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.020
Out comes an English book.

3
00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:11.540
Through a second doorway, a
different English copy appears.

4
00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:13.890
The same sentence, in both.

5
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.160
But different words light up.

6
00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:20.530
So when you quote it in your essay,
whose words are you analysing?

7
00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.930
In this mission, you'll ask who
actually made the book in your hands.

8
00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:30.180
You'll meet Keats, who knew no Greek,
discovering Homer in Chapman's version:

9
00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.430
"Much have I travell'd
in the realms of gold".

10
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:38.220
And you'll ask what, if anything,
makes it through the doorway unchanged.

11
00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:41.260
Your mission: decide whose words they are.
